# Implementation plan — live channel data, from the wire to the strip surface

Execution plan for the findings in `scripts/development/Design`. That document is
the *why* and the evidence; this one is the *what to type*, in the order it should
be typed.

Six stages. Stages 0 and 1 are independent of everything else and of each other.
Every stage is separately shippable and separately revertable — none of them
leaves the scene in a half-built state.

| Stage | What | Design ref | Workspace | Blocks |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | `catalogRevision` tracks the assembled module set | Part 2.1 | `packages/api` | 3, 4, 5 |
| 1 | `LabelFactory` generation + sweep | Part 6.6 | `client` | 4 |
| 2 | `Reading.channels` — carry the data across | Part 6.5 | `client` | 3, 4 |
| 3 | Panel: bound fields tell the truth, and a channel readout | Parts 2.2, 6.5 | `client` | 4 |
| 4 | The band ticker | Part 6.6 | `client` | — |
| 5 | Catalogue: three mis-bindings and the Tier 1 channels | Parts 3.3, 5.2 | `packages/api` | — |

