## Ground rules

Carried from `CLAUDE.md` and from the invariants the existing code already holds.
None of these is optional.

- **New backend code is TypeScript in `packages/api`.** Nothing in this plan
  touches `/api`.
- **No new types that already exist.** `SystemCoreChannel` and friends live in
  `packages/data-provider/src/types/queries.ts`; import them, do not restate them.
  Rebuild with `npm run build:data-provider` if that package changes — it does not
  in this plan.
- **No `any`. Avoid `unknown`.** The one deliberate exception is `schema.ts`, which
  validates untrusted input and documents why (`schema.ts:9-13`).
- **`live/bind.ts` and `scene/resolve.ts` must stay free of `three` and of React.**
  `resolve.ts:1-19` explains that the dialog shell imports it, so a `three` import
  there drags the whole library into the eager bundle. New file `live/ticker.ts`
  inherits the same rule.
- **The codomain invariant (`live/bind.ts:1-33`).** Anything reaching a material
  key must have a finite enumerable codomain. Stage 1 extends that guarantee to
  the label cache, which is currently outside it.
- **Single-word file names**, per `CLAUDE.md`. New files are `live/ticker.ts` and
  `Channels.tsx`.
- **Only English locale keys** are edited, in
  `client/src/locales/en/translation.json`. Other languages are automated.
- **Tests exercise real logic.** `MaterialRegistry` and `LabelFactory` both run
  under jest today — `jest-canvas-mock` is already installed and imported at
  `client/test/setupTests.js:18`, so canvas rasterisation works in tests.

