### Known behaviour this introduces

A target that flaps in and out of `up` will now add and remove its module. The
runtime map is deleted on removal (`useModules.ts:125-129`), so a flapping module
restarts its spin phase each time it returns — a visible stutter. It is confined to
*expanded* and *overflow* modules; curated catalogue entries are static and never
vanish. Accept it for now; if it proves noisy in practice the fix is a grace period
on the server, not a change on the client.

### Definition of done

`packages/api` suite green; a new scrape target reaches the scene without a reload.

