## Stage 3 — The panel tells the truth, and shows the readings

Two changes that belong together: both are "the panel stops lying about live data".

### 3a — Defect B: bound fields display the authored value

`Form.tsx:156` and `:186` pass `value={readPath(module, path)}` — the authored
module — while `boundAt` stamps the control "Driven by live data" and makes it
read-only.

**There is a wrinkle the design document did not cover, and it decides the fix.**
The controls are *uncontrolled*: `TextControl` and `NumberControl` use
`defaultValue` (`Fields.tsx:158`, `:186`), `StatusControl` seeds `useState` once
(`:215`), and the whole block only remounts when `` `${module.id}:${refillKey}` ``
changes (`Form.tsx:147`). Passing a fresh `value` prop would therefore change
nothing on screen. Folding a live hash into the key would remount every control on
every poll, destroying focus and caret position in the fields being edited.

So: **make bound controls controlled.** This is safe precisely because
`useField` (`Fields.tsx:84-99`) guarantees a bound control registers no reader —
it can never write back, so there is no commit path to disturb. `readOnly` is
already set alongside, so React raises no "value without onChange" warning.

```tsx
// Fields.tsx — NumberControl, and the same shape in TextControl
      {...(bound != null
        ? { value: value == null ? '' : String(value) }
        : { defaultValue: value == null ? '' : String(value) })}
      readOnly={bound != null}
```

`StatusControl` already renders `value={current}` from state; make that
`value={bound != null ? String(value ?? '') : current}`.

Then give `BINDINGS` the resolver, so the map stays the single place that knows
which paths the poll owns:

```ts
// live/bind.ts
export interface LiveBinding {
  channel: keyof Reading;
  name: TranslationKeys;
  /** What the panel shows for this path when there is a reading. */
  display: (m: Module, live: Reading) => unknown;
}

export const BINDINGS: Record<string, LiveBinding> = {
  status: {
    channel: 'health',
    name: 'com_ui_system_core_channel_health',
    display: effectiveStatus,
