`const` object literal evaluated at module load, not a function body.

```tsx
// Form.tsx — beside the existing boundAt
  const boundValueAt = (path: string): unknown =>
    live == null ? undefined : BINDINGS[path]?.display(module, live);

  // at both Field call sites
  value={boundValueAt(path) ?? readPath(module, path)}
```

This finally gives `readoutOf`, `effectiveHealth` and `effectiveProgress`
