## Stage 5 — Catalogue corrections and Tier 1 channels

Independent of 1–4 for *correctness*, but pointless before Stage 3, because until
something displays a channel a new one is invisible. `queries.spec.ts` fails the
build on a bundle signal with no consumer, so each operand and its channel land in
the same commit.

### 5a — Three mis-bindings (Design Part 3.3)

| Module | Now | Should be |
|---|---|---|
| `rabbitmq.throughput` | `rabbitReady` — a queue **depth** | `sum(rate(rabbitmq_channel_messages_published_total[5m]))` |
| `meilisearch.throughput` | `meiliIndexing` — a **boolean** | `sum(rate(meilisearch_http_requests_total[5m]))` |
| `kube-state-metrics.errors` | cumulative counter, climbs forever | `sum(rate(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total[15m]))` |

The rabbitmq one is the only finding in the whole audit with a genuinely misleading
visual: `throughput` reaches `boundSpeed`, so today a stalled consumer makes that
strip spin **faster**. Keep `rabbitReady` as a `connections` channel — the depth is
worth showing, it is just not a rate.

### 5b — Tier 1, in Design Part 5.2 order

Restart rate, CrashLoopBackOff, pods pending/failed, scrape-duration headroom, host
temperature, disk saturation, Rabbit consumers. Every one folds into an existing
bundle: **zero extra HTTP calls**, the 15-call constant holds.

### The one cost to watch

Bundles grow as expressions, not as requests. The per-query budget defaults to 5 s
(`systemCore/config.ts:44`) and the worst scrape already takes 1.46 s. After
each bundle grows, measure:

```bash
ssh K3s-server 'curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{time_total}\n" --get \
  --data-urlencode "query=<the extended bundle>" http://localhost:30990/api/v1/query'
```

**Measured, 2026-08-23, after all three bundles grew.** The assumption was that a
bundle of roughly twelve operands is still comfortable. It is not close to being
the binding constraint:

| Measurement | Result |
|---|---|
| Widest bundle now | `kvBundle`, 7 operands |
| Slowest single query, on the Prometheus host | 4.7 ms (`clusterBundle`) |
| Same query from this workstation, over the LAN | 43 ms |
| All 15 queries, end to end through `getSystemCoreSnapshot` | **38 ms** |
| Per-query budget (`systemCore/config.ts:44`) | 5000 ms |

Three orders of magnitude of headroom, so the 1.46 s figure above is a *scrape*
duration and not a query time — the two were easy to conflate and only one of them
is on this path. Re-measure with the command above if a bundle ever approaches a
dozen operands; nothing in Tier 2 or Tier 3 gets close.

### Tests

`catalog.spec.ts` and `queries.spec.ts` already assert the structural rules — no
backtick or `${` in any expression, every bundle signal consumed by a channel.
Extend `assemble.spec.ts` with a case per new channel resolving from a hand-built
`QueryResults`, following the existing idiom.

### Definition of done

`packages/api` suite green; new channels visible in the panel readout; total
upstream calls per snapshot still 15.

